{
  "question": "What is the federal micro-purchase threshold?",
  "status": "answered",
  "answer": "The federal micro-purchase threshold is $15,000. This rule is defined in the Federal Acquisition Regulation (FAR) 2.101. The threshold has specific exceptions, such as $2,000 for construction and $2,500 for services subject to the Service Contract Labor Standards.",
